WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 6.7 · MEAL: Monitoring, Evaluation, Accountability & Learning
Monitoring: planned versus actual

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Monitoring compares what you planned with what is actually happening, from your first activity.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:25.541
Monitoring compares what you planned with what is actually happening. For each indicator and period you record the planned value, the actual value and the gap, then ask why.

4
00:00:25.941 --> 00:00:26.541
Record, explain, then act

5
00:00:26.541 --> 00:00:38.611
Record the gap: Planned value, actual value and the difference, for each indicator and period. For example: Planned 300 loaves sold at the Saturday stall in May; actual 220; a gap of 80.

6
00:00:38.611 --> 00:00:49.570
Ask why first: Check the data, the assumptions, the context and whether the target was realistic. For example: Sales fell because the market moved our stall to a quieter corner.

7
00:00:49.570 --> 00:01:02.470
Show the status: Green on track, amber at risk, red off track, with one line of comment. For example: Amber: we ask for our old spot back and start pre-orders from June.

8
00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:03.470
Why it matters

9
00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:09.144
1. Gaps show up early, while they are still cheap to fix.

10
00:01:09.144 --> 00:01:14.078
2. Explaining before reacting stops you fixing the wrong problem.

11
00:01:14.078 --> 00:01:20.752
3. A simple dashboard keeps co-founders and partners on the same page.

12
00:01:21.152 --> 00:01:21.752
What it feeds

13
00:01:21.752 --> 00:01:26.685
1. Your learning reviews: the dashboard is the starting point.

14
00:01:26.685 --> 00:01:31.248
2. Your evaluation: monitoring data is its raw material.

15
00:01:31.248 --> 00:01:37.922
3. Your reports: planned versus actual is what funders often ask for.

16
00:01:38.322 --> 00:01:38.922
What to avoid

17
00:01:38.922 --> 00:01:43.485
Reacting to one number instead of the trend.

18
00:01:43.485 --> 00:01:47.307
Blaming people before checking the data.

19
00:01:47.307 --> 00:01:53.981
A dashboard with too many indicators to read in a minute.

20
00:01:54.581 --> 00:01:56.381
You design your monitoring dashboard and review routine.

21
00:01:56.381 --> 00:02:00.381
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

22
00:02:01.881 --> 00:02:04.981
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
